B. how fast the darkest part moves through the night as the season goes on (minutes a day by the Sun's clock; a thing fixed to the stars gives -3.9, a thing fixed to the Sun about 0)
   July to October       lit      -0.1 minutes a day, give or take 0.3 (65 nights)
   July to October       between  -0.2 minutes a day, give or take 0.3 (125 nights)
   July to October       dark     +0.3 minutes a day, give or take 0.6 (49 nights)
   August to October     lit      -0.2 minutes a day, give or take 0.4 (49 nights)
   August to October     between  -1.7 minutes a day, give or take 0.2 (96 nights)
   August to October     dark     -3.0 minutes a day, give or take 0.5 (37 nights)
   November to February  lit      -0.6 minutes a day, give or take 0.5 (21 nights)
   November to February  between  +0.9 minutes a day, give or take 0.4 (59 nights)
   November to February  dark     +2.2 minutes a day, give or take 1.0 (27 nights)
   March to June         lit      -0.6 minutes a day, give or take 0.3 (35 nights)
   March to June         between  -1.7 minutes a day, give or take 0.3 (68 nights)
   March to June         dark     -2.3 minutes a day, give or take 0.4 (22 nights)

